Ladybird keeps an extension popup between 25×25 and 800×600 CSS pixels,
sized to its page’s content. The maximum matches all three engines:
Chromium’s kExtensionPopupMaxSize, Gecko’s ExtensionPopups maxWidth and
maxHeight, and WebKit’s maximumPopoverWidth and maximumPopoverHeight.
The minimum is Chromium’s kExtensionPopupMinSize. A popup closes when
the window’s active tab changes, as Chromium’s ExtensionPopup::
OnTabStripModelChanged() closes it.
